# Bearer credential -> client id, one per line, semicolon-terminated.
#
# Copy to tokens.map (gitignored) and add real tokens with
# ./deploy/new-token.sh <client-id>. After editing:
#
#   docker compose exec nginx nginx -s reload
#
# Matching is case-INSENSITIVE: nginx lowercases both the keys in this
# file and the credential it looks up. A 40-character random token is
# still ~207 bits after case is folded away, but do not hand-write a
# token whose entropy depends on its capitalisation. The client id is
# what shows up in the nginx access log when logging is on, so make it
# something you will recognise.
# Deleting a line revokes that client on the next reload; there is no
# other state to clean up.
#
# This file is read by an nginx `map` block, so quoting matters: keep
# the credential in double quotes and end every line with a semicolon.

"replace-me-with-a-real-token"   example-client;
